{
  "slug": "compare-voucher-and-party-ledger",
  "title": "Cross-Checking a Voucher Against a Party Ledger",
  "description": "Verify that a voucher and its related ledger entry refer to the same company, party and transaction date.",
  "category": "Stock and balances",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Start from the voucher detail",
      "body": "Find the source voucher and note its party, type, number and date. This is especially useful when the business has several customer ledgers with similar names. Use the party as recorded on the document."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Trace it to the ledger period",
      "body": "Open the intended company and party ledger, and include the transaction date. Match the reference or number along with the type. If you are comparing totals, check which ledger line belongs to the transaction before comparing it with the full voucher amount."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Record a discrepancy with both views",
      "body": "If the voucher exists but you cannot identify the ledger movement, note the company, ledger and report dates and compare the original TallyPrime entry. Provide that evidence to the accountant or support team."
    }
  ],
  "relatedPaths": [
